import * as THREE from 'three';
// Twelve Apostles, target sheet 2026-10-13 - Oskar-advisor redo (project method, not the author's private code).
// Each mass is a field of jointed limestone COLUMNS on a jittered, rotated quad lattice:
//  - macro form: hand-authored lobes (headland / shoulder / tower) -> cell heights; horizontal lobe
//    combinations give shoulders and saddles, vertical ones give steps (no concentric cake tiers);
//  - constraints carve cells (rail clearance, protected volumes, town margin) - rails never move;
//  - every exposed wall is cut into vertical joint strips (per-strip inset = columns) and a few
//    block rows (subtle strata), with a wave-cut notch / cave mouths at the waterline,
//    a green drape lip under the grass rim, talus blocks, and broken rim blocks without grass;
//  - grass tables are the real cap faces; bush drifts root on them (rims, wall feet, a few meadow clumps).
